+        // tx_bps (decision 32, HARNESS-ONLY: computed at the key's read, so production pays nothing): the state slot's payload bytes per second
+        // over the transport's write ticks. Every ~33 ms write tick re-sends the latest slot (NetSyncFrames.CollectOutgoing counts the writes:
+        // StateProbe.Sends), so it is the last built payload length x the slot's sends per second, over a window of at least TxWindowMs between
+        // two key reads. Payload bytes: the 5-byte frame header is not counted. -1 = no transport, or no window yet.
