+        // ================================================================ THE MENU FINGERPRINT (decision 33)
+        // [ff9mapkit netsync s168] W1i. Stamped by the ENGINE, as the result screen stamps its _netFpOpen: fp_before at the seat (before anything
+        // is installed: the guest's own state), fp_after at the restore (after every family is back); the verdict is fp_after == fp_before, never
+        // read while seated. seat_fp over the installed, seated copy (stamped at the seat; from s169 at C's re-seat); host_fp over the host's own
+        // live state, HARNESS-ONLY (W1d stamps it inside HostGuestMenuSectionNow's try; StampHostFp returns at once unless HarnessAgent.Active).
+        // One 64-bit word per COMPONENT (FNV-1a 64's offset basis and prime, one step per VALUE: see MixU), read-only and in-engine, over every
